mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# DeFi yield tracker backend API\n\nThis canister stores each signed-in user's private DeFi data: settings, a pool watchlist, tracked positions, tracked wallet addresses, price/yield alert rules and an alert history. It also evaluates alert rules on a schedule using public DefiLlama pool data (no API key), sends alert emails to the user's verified Internet Identity email, and mints short-lived AI inference keys for the browser. Pool market data itself is NOT served by this canister; the frontend reads public sources directly.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- Every per-user method below traps for the anonymous principal (message such as `Anonymous callers are not allowed`). Call them with a signed-in (non-anonymous) identity.\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization must derive the per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). A principal derived against a different origin is a different user with different, empty data.\n- Warning: such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires, including `deleteAllMyData`.\n- Data isolation: every record is stored under the caller's principal. A caller can read and change only their own rows. There is no admin read access to other users' rows through this API.\n- Registration prerequisite: the authorization mixin registers a caller only when the caller signs in through the app's own frontend (which calls `_initialize_access_control`). The per-user methods in this document do not require that registration, only a non-anonymous principal. The first caller to initialize access control becomes admin and later callers become users; role-guarded admin methods of the authorization mixin trap with an `Unauthorized` message for unregistered or anonymous callers.\n- Verified email: when a user signs in through the app frontend with an Internet Identity that carries a verified email (Google or Microsoft backed), the email is captured automatically and used only for alert emails. It is never returned by any method. `hasVerifiedEmail` reports whether one is stored. Users cannot type in an address.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- Timestamps (`entryTimestamp`, `createdAt`, `lastTriggeredAt`, `triggeredAt`) are `Int` nanoseconds since the Unix epoch. Convert milliseconds to nanoseconds by multiplying by 1,000,000.\n- `amountUsd` is a `Float` in US dollars and must be greater than 0 and below 1e15.\n- APY values, thresholds for `#apyBelow` and `#apyAbove`, and `observedValue` are percent numbers (`3.5` means 3.5%).\n- `#tvlDropPercent` threshold is a percent in the range greater than 0 up to 100, measured as the TVL decrease versus roughly 24 hours earlier.\n- `poolId` is the public DefiLlama pool UUID (the `{poolId}` of `yields.llama.fi/chart/{poolId}`). For alert rules it may contain only letters, digits, `-` and `_`, up to 100 characters.\n- Ids (`id`, `ruleId`) are `Nat`. Optional values (`notes`, `lastTriggeredAt`) are Candid `opt`. Variants: `Theme = #dark | #light | #auto`; `AlertMetric = #apyBelow | #apyAbove | #tvlDropPercent`.\n- Text fields are limited to 200 characters (`notes` to 1000).\n\n## Errors\n\n- Failures the caller can fix return `Result` with `#err` carrying `ApiError = #notFound | #invalid : Text | #limitReached : Nat` (the Nat is the limit that was hit).\n- Anonymous callers trap (the call is rejected). Traps roll back the call.\n- Limits per user: 100 watchlist entries, 200 positions, 20 wallets, 25 alert rules, newest 200 alert history entries kept.\n\n## Methods: account and settings\n\n- `hasVerifiedEmail() : Bool` (query). True when an Internet Identity verified email was captured for the caller.\n- `getSettings() : Settings` (query). `Settings = { emailAlertsEnabled : Bool; autoRefreshEnabled : Bool; theme : Theme }`. Returns defaults (`emailAlertsEnabled = true`, `autoRefreshEnabled = true`, `theme = #dark`) before the first save.\n- `updateSettings(Settings) : ()`. Replaces the caller's settings. Idempotent.\n- `deleteAllMyData() : ()`. Permanently deletes the caller's settings, watchlist, positions, wallets, alert rules and alert history. Destructive and irreversible; calling it again is harmless. The stored verified email is kept so alerts can resume.\n- `getInferenceCredentials()` is described under AI access below.\n\n## Methods: watchlist\n\n- `listWatchlist() : [WatchlistEntry]` (query). `WatchlistEntry = { poolId; displayName; symbol; project; chain }`, all Text.\n- `addToWatchlist(WatchlistEntry) : Result<(), ApiError>`. Upsert by `poolId`: re-adding refreshes the stored details, so retries are safe. `#limitReached(100)` when full.\n- `removeFromWatchlist(poolId : Text) : Bool`. True if an entry was removed; false if it did not exist.\n\n## Methods: positions\n\n- `listPositions() : [Position]` (query). `Position = { id; poolId; displayName; symbol; amountUsd; entryTimestamp; notes : ?Text }`.\n- `addPosition(PositionInput) : Result<Position, ApiError>`. `PositionInput` is a Position without `id`. NOT idempotent: every successful call creates a new position with a new id, so do not blindly retry after an unknown outcome; list positions first.\n- `updatePosition(id : Nat, PositionInput) : Result<Position, ApiError>`. Replaces the position; `#notFound` for an unknown id. Idempotent.\n- `removePosition(id : Nat) : Bool`. True if removed.\n\n## Methods: tracked wallets\n\nWallets are saved addresses only. The canister does not read chains or import balances.\n\n- `listWallets() : [TrackedWallet]` (query). `TrackedWallet = { address : Text; chain : Text }`.\n- `addWallet(TrackedWallet) : Result<(), ApiError>`. Idempotent per chain plus address (EVM `0x` addresses compare case-insensitively). `#limitReached(20)` when full.\n- `removeWallet(chain : Text, address : Text) : Bool`.\n\n## Methods: import from the browser\n\n- `importLocalData(ImportBatch) : ImportSummary`. `ImportBatch = { watchlist : [WatchlistEntry]; positions : [PositionInput]; wallets : [TrackedWallet] }`. Merges data into the caller's saved data, skipping invalid items, duplicates (same pool id for watchlist; same pool id plus entry timestamp for positions; same chain plus address for wallets) and items beyond the per-user limits. `ImportSummary = { watchlistAdded; positionsAdded; walletsAdded; skipped }`. Safe to retry: repeats are skipped.\n\n## Methods: alert rules and history\n\nAlert rule: `{ id; poolId; poolLabel; metric; threshold; enabled; armed; createdAt; lastTriggeredAt : ?Int }`. Rule input: `{ poolId; poolLabel; metric; threshold }` (`poolLabel` 1 to 120 characters).\n\n- `createAlertRule(AlertRuleInput) : Result<AlertRule, ApiError>`. Creates an enabled, armed rule. Not idempotent: each call adds a new rule (maximum 25).\n- `updateAlertRule(id : Nat, AlertRuleInput) : Result<AlertRule, ApiError>`. Replaces the rule's pool, metric and threshold and re-arms it. `#notFound` for unknown id.\n- `setAlertRuleEnabled(id : Nat, enabled : Bool) : Result<AlertRule, ApiError>`. Enabling a disabled rule re-arms it. Idempotent.\n- `deleteAlertRule(id : Nat) : Bool`.\n- `listAlertRules() : [AlertRule]` (query).\n- `listAlertHistory() : [AlertHistoryEntry]` (query), newest first. `AlertHistoryEntry = { id; ruleId; poolLabel; metric; observedValue; threshold; triggeredAt; read : Bool; emailSent : Bool }`. At most 200 entries are kept per user.\n- `unreadAlertCount() : Nat` (query).\n- `markAlertRead(id : Nat) : Bool`, `markAllAlertsRead() : ()`, `clearAlertHistory() : ()`. All idempotent.\n- `evaluateMyAlertsNow() : EvaluationSummary`. Update call that fetches DefiLlama chart data for the caller's enabled rules immediately and evaluates them. `EvaluationSummary = { rulesEvaluated; triggered; failedPools }`. It makes outbound HTTPS calls and can take several seconds; do not call it in a tight loop.\n\n### Alert lifecycle (armed, triggered, re-armed)\n\n1. A new or re-enabled or edited rule is `enabled = true`, `armed = true`.\n2. A background timer evaluates every user's enabled rules about every 30 minutes (and `evaluateMyAlertsNow` does it on demand). Conditions: `#apyBelow` fires when the pool's latest APY is below the threshold; `#apyAbove` when it is above; `#tvlDropPercent` when TVL fell by at least the threshold percent versus about 24 hours earlier.\n3. When the condition is met on an armed rule, the rule becomes triggered: `armed = false`, `lastTriggeredAt` is set, one history entry is written (`read = false`), and, if the user has a verified email and `emailAlertsEnabled`, one email is sent (`emailSent` reports whether it was accepted).\n4. A triggered (unarmed) rule does not fire again while the condition holds. It re-arms automatically the next time an evaluation finds the condition no longer met.\n5. If pool data cannot be fetched, the rule is left unchanged and counted in `failedPools`.\n\n### Polling guidance\n\nThere is no push channel. To see new alerts, poll `unreadAlertCount` (a cheap query) or `listAlertHistory` no more often than about once a minute. New history entries appear only after the scheduled run (every 30 minutes) or an `evaluateMyAlertsNow` call.\n\n## AI access\n\n- `getInferenceCredentials() : Credentials` mints a short-lived inference key (valid about 3 hours, reused for about 15 minutes per caller, limited to 30 mints per caller per hour) so the browser can call the hosted chat completions API directly. Signed-in callers only; anonymous callers trap with `Sign in to use AI features`. Treat the returned key as a secret: keep it in memory only, never persist or log it. There is no backend chat method. A canister upgrade revokes all minted keys; request new credentials when the gateway answers 401.\n\n## Data queries (OQL)\n\n- `schema()` and `execute(query : Text)` expose the tables `settings`, `watchlist`, `position`, `wallet`, `alertRule` and `alertHistory` for read-only structured queries. Each table is scoped per user: a signed-in caller sees only their own rows (every row has an `owner` principal column). Anonymous callers are denied. Money is in USD, timestamps are nanoseconds since the Unix epoch, and `theme` and `metric` are returned as text tags.\n\n## Other endpoints\n\n- `transform` is an internal query callback required by HTTPS outcalls. Do not call it.\n- Authorization mixin methods (for example `_initialize_access_control`, `getCallerUserRole`, `isCallerAdmin`, `assignCallerUserRole`) manage roles. They are not needed to use the per-user methods above.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- Demo or fallback data shown in the frontend is never stored here; only data you save through these methods persists.\n- Float values are IEEE doubles: avoid comparing them for exact equality.\n- Amounts and APY are not currency-converted; amounts are USD only."
  };
};
